{
 "id": "2026-11-27-flinders-island-fire",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A tenth of an Australian island has burned. Summer has not even started."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Flinders Island, off Tasmania. The fire started near Palana on November nineteenth, likely from lightning. After a wind change on Wednesday, it grew about fourfold in a day, reports say. ABC News says almost fifteen thousand hectares have burned."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Around eight buildings are damaged or destroyed, ABC reports, some homes. Authorities warned some residents refused to evacuate. On Friday, the national fire authorities council flagged higher bushfire risk this summer in parts of every state and territory, except Queensland and Canberra's territory."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "It cites heavy fuel loads, dry soils and a hot, dry forecast. The weather bureau expects a hotter than average summer for almost all of Australia. It says El Niño is strengthening, with models suggesting a peak around December or January."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Flinders Island fire be out before summer starts? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
