  "title": "A Tenth of Tasmania's Flinders Island Has Burned #shorts",
  "description": "A bushfire on Flinders Island, off Tasmania, has burned almost 15,000 hectares, more than 10% of the island, ABC News reports; around eight buildings, some of them homes, are damaged or destroyed (preliminary). On Friday, AFAC's summer outlook flagged increased bushfire risk in parts of every state and territory except Queensland and the ACT, and the Bureau of Meteorology expects a hotter than average summer for almost all of Australia as El Niño strengthens.\n\nSources: ABC News (Australia); SBS News; The New Daily; Weatherzone; news.com.au; AFAC Seasonal Bushfire Outlook; Bureau of Meteorology (based on search-result excerpts). Fire, risk and heat areas on the map are approximate and illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #bushfire #australia #elnino",
